From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter B Hough <git@hough.ink>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 19:17:07 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 154/171] test(gastown): test_polecat_artifact_dir.sh passes on
 darwin and tracks the current formulas (gcp-xveoh)

The suite exited 1 on macOS at its first case ("valid per-bead legacy
worktree was rejected"). Cause, from a bash -x run: the validator's
redirected-rig-namespace guard, mol-polecat-work.toml:379
([ "$rig_namespace_real" = "$rig_namespace" ]), compared
/private/var/folders/.../city-a/.gc/worktrees/demo against
/var/folders/.../city-a/.gc/worktrees/demo. The test built city_a from
mktemp -d, which returns /var/folders/... on macOS even with TMPDIR under
/private/tmp, and /var is a symlink to /private/var. The product callers
(workspace-setup, task-artifact-cleanup.sh) resolve the city root with
pwd -P before they reach the validator, so this was the harness handing it
an unresolved root. Product code is unchanged: resolving both sides would
defeat the guard, which exists to reject a symlinked rig namespace.

Fixing the first case exposed that the rest of the file had drifted from
the formulas it reads, on any host, because CI does not gate this suite on
integration:

- Every mktemp -d now goes through physical_mktemp_dir.
- extract_workspace_creation took the first five bash blocks of
  workspace-setup; the work-bead claim added a sixth, so the extracted
  script stopped before the worktree was created. It now takes everything
  up to the block that runs "worktree add".
- The four workspace tests' gc stubs predate the claim and the step-1
  handoff_stage/base_ref writes. They now accept the claim call and pin
  BEADS_ACTOR, so the expected call no longer depends on the session that
  runs the suite.
- sed -i with a script argument is a GNU-only form (BSD sed reads it as the
  backup suffix); replaced with sed to a file and mv.
- The refinery cleanup contract asserted prose in the merge-push step that
  gcp-fooz4 moved into refinery/merge-push.sh. The assertions now read the
  script, and the prose ones became structural: no cleanup on the PR
  publication path, merge evidence recorded before the close, cleanup only
  after the MR head lands, no source-ref deletion.

Validation: bash gastown/tests/test_polecat_artifact_dir.sh exits 0 on
darwin, all 15 cases in one run.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
